<p>President Trump said the war with Iran could be over &quot;very soon&quot; and that a second round of U.S.-Iran talks could happen within days, likely again in Pakistan, as mediators tried to keep diplomacy moving. He made those comments while a two-week ceasefire remains in place and after earlier talks in Islamabad ended without a breakthrough, leaving the core dispute over Iran’s nuclear program unresolved. At the same time, the U.S. military said it had fully implemented a blockade on Iranian maritime trade, using naval forces to stop shipping to and from Iranian ports while keeping the Strait of Hormuz open to broader traffic. Iran warned that the blockade could jeopardize the ceasefire and threatened to disrupt other regional sea lanes, though reports also said Tehran was weighing ways to avoid derailing talks and had floated proposals to let ships pass on the Oman side of Hormuz if a deal is reached. The standoff matters far beyond the Gulf because Hormuz carries roughly 20% of global oil and liquefied natural gas flows. That makes any progress in talks a rare source of hope for regional stability and for world energy markets already strained by weeks of conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/jdXZICUAa_IsYuPZW8q5Zd_mavGBv_XNHnEsyp7mYzaGqlNT2E1cUqhmuR_1S_QQnkhwZtQdYC4HGp2GEaJqDhrgSoE3GBQ_tdrJ9PJ9mmI4kAWhJc9wPNtGe2FR6JHmSBt3ZzujXVk9vKSqj8oREvtQCWp9EalGMEUO_A2R3bRCIfxwX9NAH_yDm1nUcLEmMKodJHico7sbDdnLt5MXfQ' alt='A vessel at the Strait of Hormuz, off the coast of Oman’s Musandam province, on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ceasefire denial: White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt said reports that Washington had requested a ceasefire were false, even as she described discussions on a new round of talks as ongoing and productive.</li><li>Ships turned back: U.S. officials said nine vessels turned back within 48 hours of the blockade, while maritime data and Iranian media suggested some tankers still transited nearby international waters with tracking systems on.</li><li>Market pressure: Oil prices fell for a second straight day as hopes for renewed talks grew, even though Politico reported that high oil and gasoline prices were still roiling the global economy.</li><li>Extension murky: The Hindu cited regional officials saying Washington and Tehran had an “in principle agreement” to extend the ceasefire beyond April 22 and allow more diplomacy.</li><li>Regional spillover: Even as U.S.-Iran truce talks advanced, Israel continued military operations against Iran-backed Hezbollah in Lebanon, underscoring that broader regional tensions remain unresolved.</li></ul><blockquote>I think it can be over very soon. If they’re smart, it will end soon. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: Washington is trying to publicly separate ceasefire politics from negotiations, denying that it asked for a ceasefire while still describing contacts on a second round as ongoing and productive. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/white-house-denies-us-requested-ceasefire-says-new-talks-may-happen-pakistan'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iranian officials warn that the blockade threatens the ceasefire and say they could retaliate by disrupting shipping in the Red Sea, Gulf, and Sea of Oman if U.S. pressure continues. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/15/iran-warns-us-naval-blockade-threatens-ceasefire'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistan’s military leadership is unusually driving the mediation effort, with army chief Asim Munir in Tehran and mediators still voicing hope for a breakthrough on the nuclear issue. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/trump-peace-talks-iran-blockade-china-russia/33732708.html'>RFE/RL</a>, <a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/15/pakistan-army-chief-in-tehran-to-advance-next-round-of-us-iran-talks'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Analysts: Analysts cited by the South China Morning Post say Trump’s public optimism reflects pressure to break a military and political deadlock while a negotiated exit still remains possible. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3350201/trump-says-iran-war-close-over-he-just-out-options'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638440-trump-iran-us-talks/'>End of Iran war ‘very close’ – Trump</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-says-iran-war-very-close-to-being-over-as-us-blockades-iranian-ports'>Trump says Iran war close to being over as US blockades Iranian ports</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/trump-says-iran-war-is-at-a-brink-of-being-over-ahead-of-fresh-peace-talks-11360476#publisher=newsstand'>Trump Says Iran War Is At A Brink Of &quot;Being Over&quot;, Ahead Of Fresh Peace Talks</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/trump-peace-talks-iran-blockade-china-russia/33732708.html'>Trump Says War Could End &#x27;Very Soon,&#x27; Top Mediator Travels To Iran</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3350201/trump-says-iran-war-close-over-he-just-out-options'>Trump says the Iran war is ‘close to over’. Is he just out of options?</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/15/trump-says-iran-war-very-close-to-over-as-truce-talks-advance'>Trump says Iran war &#x27;very close to over&#x27; as truce talks advance</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/trump-iran-war-strait-hormuz-ceasefire-pakistan-peace-talks-israel-lebanon/'>Trump says Iran war &quot;close to over&quot; amid push for new peace talks</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-pakistan-attempts-to-mediate-as-trump-says-iran-war-nearly-over/'>Pakistan attempts to mediate as Trump says Iran war nearly over</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/202